rain-core: xray/0051-muxcool-pool-lifecycle
Source: ReClash fix on top of xray/0037 (GPL-3.0).

The shared carrier dial inherited the context of whichever caller happened to
start it, so one request timing out aborted the carrier that every other
waiter needed. The dial now belongs to the pool: a value-preserving context
detached from the caller, a 30 s pool dial timeout, one dial at a time, and
the error delivered to the waiters of that dial. Repeated failures back off
(100 ms doubling to 2 s, the first failure retried at once) so a mass carrier
loss does not turn every new session into another dial.

The carrier limiter now registers its pools. When every slot is taken, a
waiter asks all pools to close carriers that have been idle past a one-second
grace, instead of waiting up to the 16 s idle timeout for the other pool to
release a carrier; a just-freed carrier stays available for reuse in its own
pool.

Tests: TestCanceledInitiatorDoesNotAbortSharedCarrierDial,
TestCarrierLimiterReclaimsIdleCarrierOfAnotherPool,
TestPoolDoesNotStormCarrierDialsAfterRepeatedFailures.
